{
  "title": "Course Project: Pharmacological Characterization of Novel Agents",
  "body": "Students will design a study to characterize a hypothetical or real drug candidate based on the principles of receptor pharmacology and dose-response relationships. The project requires students to define the drug's efficacy, potency, and selectivity, and to construct theoretical dose-response curves. Students must distinguish between graded and quantal responses and explain the clinical relevance of these parameters. The final deliverable will include a proposal outlining the experimental approach, a discussion of expected outcomes regarding affinity and intrinsic activity, and an analysis of potential side effects based on drug selectivity. This project reinforces the core concepts introduced in Lecture 1, including the definitions of agonists, antagonists, and the sigmoidal nature of dose-response curves.",
